From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: on AMD the GPU process preloads Google's DRI driver
 from /usr/lib64/cros

NickelOS Unified's Mesa is Gentoo's 26: dri/radeonsi_dri.so is a stub that
loads libgallium, and there is no libglapi. The AMD preload before the GPU
sandbox asked for libglapi.so and failed, and the sandbox with it.
minigbm's amdgpu backend still allocates through the DRI interface of
Google's radeonsi driver, which the image keeps for it alone in
/usr/lib64/cros/dri with its libglapi beside it, linked -Bsymbolic. The
GPU process now preloads that driver the way minigbm's patch 0002 loads
it, RTLD_LOCAL (and RTLD_NODELETE, as before), so none of its symbols
become everyone's: Gentoo's Mesa, which loads inside the sandbox (0078),
keeps its own (the AMD test PC, 2026-10-20).

diff --git a/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc b/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
index 2c96f4b4c8d05..a47abb3335328 100644
--- a/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
+++ b/content/common/gpu_pre_sandbox_hook_linux.cc
@@ -592,17 +592,19 @@ void LoadArmGpuLibraries() {
 }
 
 bool LoadAmdGpuLibraries() {
-  // Preload the amdgpu-dependent libraries.
-  if (nullptr == dlopen("libglapi.so", dlopen_flag)) {
-    LOG(ERROR) << "dlopen(libglapi.so) failed with error: " << dlerror();
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  const char* radeonsi_lib = "/usr/lib64/dri/radeonsi_dri.so";
-#if defined(DRI_DRIVER_DIR)
-  radeonsi_lib = DRI_DRIVER_DIR "/radeonsi_dri.so";
-#endif
-  if (nullptr == dlopen(radeonsi_lib, dlopen_flag)) {
+  // NickelOS: Mesa is Gentoo's. Its dri/radeonsi_dri.so is a stub that
+  // loads libgallium, and it has no libglapi: this preload failed at
+  // libglapi.so, and with it the sandbox. minigbm's amdgpu backend still
+  // allocates through the DRI interface of Google's driver, kept for it
+  // alone in /usr/lib64/cros/dri with its libglapi beside it and linked
+  // -Bsymbolic, so its calls to its own functions stay its own (Gentoo's
+  // libgallium exports some of the same names). Load it as minigbm does
+  // (its patch 0002): RTLD_LOCAL, so none of its symbols become
+  // everyone's and Gentoo's Mesa, which loads inside the sandbox
+  // (AddNickelMesaPermissions), keeps its own.
+  const char kRadeonsiLib[] = "/usr/lib64/cros/dri/radeonsi_dri.so";
+  if (nullptr ==
+      dlopen(kRadeonsiLib, RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL | RTLD_NODELETE)) {
     LOG(ERROR) << "dlopen(radeonsi_dri.so) failed with error: " << dlerror();
     return false;
   }
